    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-29179: sec x=2 means cos x=1/2; the permitted angles are -300° and -60°, whose numerical product is 18000. The source's x3 label is an indexing typo that does not affect its final answer. q-76503 and q-29163: the real secant range excludes (-1,1), so respectively only equation I (sec x=0) and equation III (sec x=1/2) have no solutions. q-28519: real coefficients require the conjugate root (-2-7i)/2. q-28523: 3(x-2i)(x+2i)=3x²+12. q-28215: (x+1-i)(x+1+i)=x²+2x+2. q-16935: 4[(x-1/2)²+3]=4x²-4x+13. q-32705: dx/dy=4/y³+4y, so dy/dx=y³/(4+4y⁴), with y≠0 as required by the original expression. q-170140: dy/dx=1/(1-6y²), giving -1/5 at y=-1. q-32595: dx/dy=y^(-1/2)+(3/2)y^(-3/2), giving dy/dx=18/7 at y=9. q-32596: dx/dy=2y²-2y=12 at y=3, so y-3=(x-9)/12 and y=x/12+9/4. q-110192: dx/dy=15y²-16y=28 at y=2, so y-2=(x-24)/28 and y=x/28+8/7. q-1783: P(15,4)=15·14·13·12=32760. q-122228: assigning distinct employees to the three distinct shifts gives 9·8·7=504. q-72824: the angles are π-arctan(8) and 2π-arctan(8), approximately 1.6952 and 4.8367; their product rounds to 8.2. q-120828: the angles are arcsin(2/3)≈41.8103° and 180°-41.8103°≈138.1897°, rounding to 42° and 138°. Selected choice expressions are equivalent to the source answers; alignment syntax and numerical spacing do not alter their values.",
